1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,690
JIEJING is a beginner-friendly Grasshopper toolkit for creating fabrication-ready Chinese lattice windows from traditional geometry and optional personal images.

2
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:17,549
The workflow starts with a window boundary. In the Baby Starter, every component is already connected, so a new user can begin by changing the width and height.

3
00:00:17,549 --> 00:00:28,452
Fourteen built-in recipes provide different geometric families. Density, lattice weight, and frame weight remain parametric, allowing one rule to adapt to different windows and materials.

4
00:00:28,452 --> 00:00:39,346
Borrowed View introduces intentional openness instead of filling the entire panel. The user can choose a traditional profile, such as begonia, plum, ruyi, fan, or gourd.

5
00:00:39,346 --> 00:00:49,377
The same cat image is used throughout this demonstration. This is not generative AI. The plugin extracts contrast and edge information, then maps it to repeated lattice cells.

6
00:00:49,377 --> 00:00:59,840
Silhouette, portrait-detail, and hybrid modes balance recognition and geometric continuity. Image strength and polarity provide further control while keeping the result editable.

7
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:07,909
The material preview shows black as material that remains and white as openings to be cut. Check connectivity and member width before fabrication.

8
00:01:07,909 --> 00:01:17,071
One switch exports one-to-one DXF, SVG, and PDF files, moving from a personal image to an editable and manufacturable window screen.
